config STEALTH_NET
	bool "Stealth In-Kernel DNS/SNI Engine"
	depends on NETFILTER && INET && CRYPTO && NF_CONNTRACK
	select CRYPTO_AES
	select CRYPTO_ECB
	select CRYPTO_GCM
	select CRYPTO_HMAC
	select CRYPTO_SHA256
	default y
	help
	  In-kernel network inspector and modifier.
	  Provides stealth DNS blocking, spoofing, and TLS SNI audit.
	  Optional ghost modes reject unsolicited inbound traffic, suppress
	  local discovery and protect learned ARP/NDP neighbour mappings.
	  Provides bounded TCP telemetry, VPN MSS clamping and optional TCP
	  hardening without tracepoint dependencies.
	  Provides an opt-in, metadata-only /proc capture stream with UID,
	  interface, direction and firewall verdict attribution.
	  Includes an opt-in local IDS with scan detection, canary ports,
	  trusted peers and expiring source bans.
	  Includes an opt-in userspace tunnel leak guard. It can audit or
	  fail closed unless application traffic uses a configured TUN
	  interface, while exempting the configured relay daemon UID.
	  Includes /proc/stealth_dns and /proc/stealth_events interfaces.

	  If unsure, say Y.
